    "question": "Ten percent less than twice the total number of students present in the science class yesterday have attended class today. If there were 70 students in the class yesterday and 30 students are absent today, calculate the number of students registered for the course.",
    "question_sha256": "c29b852b5702640b5fea41acceef3d57783a18a695d46b4badec1a74ec0c0ed8",
    "responses": [
      {
        "key": "gsm8k-train-4310:rich",
        "raw_call_sha256": "8cd38612fca81f52c7ae3353473a634eeccd723819f2772128da483b88359f53",
        "student_prefix": [
          {
            "content": "Ten percent less than twice the total number of students present in the science class yesterday have attended class today. If there were 70 students in the class yesterday and 30 students are absent today, calculate the number of students registered for the course.",
            "role": "user"
          }
        ],
        "student_prefix_sha256": "4abe44a7a7f63633efac3190909bf1266cd8199d067a8924f0c4860fc957e9a5",
        "target": "Given:\n- 10% less than twice the number of students present yesterday have attended today.\n- Yesterday, there were 70 students.\n- Today, 30 students are absent.\n\nFirst, calculate twice the number of students from yesterday:\n2 * 70 = 140\n\nNext, find 10% of 140:\n10% of 140 = 0.10 * 140 = 14\n\nNow, subtract this 10% from 140 to get the number of students who attended today:\n140 - 14 = 126\n\nSince 30 students are absent today, the total number of students registered for the course is:\n126 (present today) + 30 (absent today) = 156\n\nFINAL: 156",
